The following sets are admissible by Theorem <<ref:thm:dgactylp>> and Theorem <<ref:rr>>.

$$ [(i)]\ \
\begin{tabular}{c c }
\xymatrix @C=0.1em {
(k,i+1,j) \ar[rd]& &    &    \\
& (k,i,j)    & &    \\
}
\end{tabular}
\ \ [(ii)]\ \
\begin{tabular}{c c }
\xymatrix @C=0.1em {
& &  (k,i+1,j)\ar[rd]   & &   \\
& (k,i,j)  \ar[ru]\ar[rd]   & &(k,i,j+1)   \\
&     &(k,i-1,j)\ar[ru]  &   \\
}
\end{tabular}$$

$ [(iii)] \ \begin{tabular}{c c } \xymatrix @C=0.1em { & & (k,i+1,j+1) &

& (k,i,j) \ar[ru] & &

} \end{tabular} $

It follows from Lemma <<ref:lemma permutation>> that the permutations of these sets are also admissible.
